+/*
+ * RK3308BS EVB (Artillery M1 Pro S1-SOC) GT911 fold-fix + single-touch clamp.
+ *
+ * This board's GT911 reports its HORIZONTAL axis (chip-native X, the first
+ * coordinate word) in a folded "double-width" space: a hard dead gap that the
+ * chip never emits at native X [350..749], with two reachable bands [50..349]
+ * and [750..1079]. The VERTICAL axis (chip-native Y, second word) is linear
+ * over roughly [588..1741]. The fold is intrinsic to the digitizer (identical
+ * under mainline goodix, the vendor gt9xx driver, the chip's own config, and
+ * the genuine factory firmware), so it is corrected in software here.
+ *
+ * The chip also frequently emits a spurious second "phantom" contact near the
+ * fold. This is a single-touch product (480x272 KlipperScreen panel); the
+ * factory firmware tolerates the phantom only because its LVGL GUI consumes a
+ * single contact. Under X11/libinput the phantom is promoted to bogus
+ * pinch/scroll gestures. We therefore report only the dominant contact
+ * (largest touch-major width == strongest capacitance == the real finger,
+ * matching the controller's own arbitration), unfolded, always in slot 0.
+ */
+#define RK3308BS_FOLD_FIX	1
+/*
+ * Horizontal (folded) axis calibration LUT. The GT911 reports this axis in two
+ * folded bands whose physical scales are DIFFERENT and individually non-linear
+ * (a ruler tap capture, one tap per cm, was used). A simple two-slope model
+ * left a mid-band sag, so we instead store the measured (chip-x -> output)
+ * calibration points and linearly interpolate between them. This maps chip x
+ * to a coordinate linear in physical position over 0..RK3308BS_Y_MAX.
+ * Points are ordered by ascending chip x; output DEscends (higher chip x =
+ * further left = smaller output). Refine by editing these pairs from a fresh
+ * ruler calibration.
+ */
+#define RK3308BS_Y_MAX		629	/* unfolded horizontal (ABS_MT_POSITION_X after rotate) max */
+#define RK3308BS_X_MIN		588	/* vertical linear min */
+#define RK3308BS_X_MAX		1153	/* vertical span 1741-588 (ABS_MT_POSITION_Y after rotate) max */
+
